Applicable upstream post-2.3.2 parser follow-ups adapted to the 1.x offset
and iterator APIs: overflow-safe FLAC picture and ByteVector bounds, Ogg page
and stream replacement bounds, text value budgets and linear genre parsing.
Keep the 1.x APIs and C++11 language level.
Upstream commits: https://github.com/taglib/taglib/commit/<full ID below>.

From 8fe8b8235b857fcaee6d16a9561e9659c5628fe4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Acts1631 <69813585+acts-1631@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:17:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Prevent FLAC picture length overflows (#1492)

FLAC picture string and data lengths were checked with addition. On
32-bit builds, crafted lengths can wrap the cursor and cause a
four-byte read before the ByteVector allocation.

Use remaining-length checks in Picture::parse and make fixed-width
ByteVector conversions reject offsets at or beyond the buffer.

From 58499cb157c38b8d07b262b15c4ecba9f36aeb9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Acts1631 <69813585+acts-1631@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 23:43:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Fix ByteVector bounds checks (#1493)

ByteVector::endsWith underflows when the pattern is longer than the
receiver. containsAt then uses an addition that can wrap, allowing an
out-of-bounds memcmp and a process crash.

Reject invalid pattern offsets before subtraction and compare against
the remaining receiver length without overflowing.

From 1819fda4800af68bf688c7e111504f36f0ea5854 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Acts1631 <69813585+acts-1631@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 11:07:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Validate Ogg page bounds before saving (#1491)

Ogg page lacing values can declare payload beyond EOF. During an
in-memory tag update, that replacement span can underflow the length
passed to memmove and crash the process.

Reject truncated pages and make ByteVectorStream::insert ignore invalid
replacement ranges before doing offset arithmetic.

From 5bd11b2fb6009eb35712dd6663c22ddea79f6a58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Acts1631 <69813585+acts-1631@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:28:51 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Bound text value counts in ID3v2 and APE tags (#1458)

Null-separated text values create a ByteVector and String for each
tiny field. A 1 MB tag can allocate over 100 MB and abort
memory-limited applications.

Limit decoded values based on input size and stop before creating
String objects when the value count exceeds the budget.

From 62db51159d543cd3eca08d33150621544d7be84e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Acts1631 <69813585+acts-1631@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 14:28:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Avoid repeated genre suffix copies in ID3v2 parsing (#1457)

A TCON frame with many legacy genre codes copies the remaining text
for every code. A small crafted tag can consume seconds of CPU.

Walk the original string by offset, compare mapped genres without
copying the suffix, and limit decoded codes by input size.

--- a/taglib/ape/apeitem.cpp
+++ b/taglib/ape/apeitem.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@
  *   http://www.mozilla.org/MPL/                                           *
  ***************************************************************************/
 
+#include <algorithm>
 #include <tbytevectorlist.h>
 #include <tdebug.h>
 
@@ -259,8 +260,18 @@
   setReadOnly(flags & 1);
   setType(static_cast<ItemTypes>((flags >> 1) & 3));
 
-  if(Text == d->type)
-    d->text = StringList(ByteVectorList::split(value, '\0'), String::UTF8);
+  if(Text == d->type) {
+    static const unsigned int MAX_TEXT_VALUE_COUNT = 50000;
+    const unsigned int maxValues = std::min(MAX_TEXT_VALUE_COUNT,
+      std::max(1024U, value.size() / 32));
+    const ByteVectorList values = ByteVectorList::split(
+      value, '\0', 1, static_cast<int>(maxValues + 1));
+    if(values.size() > maxValues) {
+      debug("APE::Item::parse() -- Maximum text value count exceeded");
+      return;
+    }
+    d->text = StringList(values, String::UTF8);
+  }
   else
     d->value = value;
 }
